WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.930
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:34.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs

01:35.030 --> 01:40.080
Episode 7:
Another Family

02:27.280 --> 02:29.700
What a big city!
- This is Bordeaux.

02:29.970 --> 02:31.330
Bordeaux?
- Yes.

02:49.780 --> 02:51.260
Thank you, madame.

03:12.040 --> 03:14.340
Mr. Vitalis, umm...

03:15.280 --> 03:16.650
Can I go see the boats?

03:17.030 --> 03:20.020
I've never seen so many boats.

03:20.220 --> 03:23.460
It's okay, as long as you come back before dinner.

03:24.390 --> 03:27.830
Okay.
- And... take Capi with you.

03:31.240 --> 03:33.400
Huh? You want to come too?

03:34.530 --> 03:36.660
All right, let's go!

03:39.490 --> 03:41.710
You stay here, Joli-Coeur.

03:52.050 --> 03:55.620
These are some really big ships.
I wonder where they're going?

03:56.190 --> 03:57.620
I'd like to travel by boat.

04:08.690 --> 04:12.000
Do you like dogs?
- Who are you?

04:12.220 --> 04:17.070
I'm Remy, and you?
- Me? I'm Emile.

04:17.420 --> 04:19.870
Captain of the Prima Vela.

04:23.640 --> 04:26.680
I'm only joking, I'm just a sailor.

04:28.860 --> 04:31.480
Are these your companions?
- Yes.

04:31.880 --> 04:35.050
The big one is Capi and the little one is Dolce.

04:35.690 --> 04:38.360
We're members of the Vitalis troupe.

04:38.870 --> 04:41.840
Tomorrow in the town square we'll be doing performances.

04:41.950 --> 04:44.640
Oh, that sounds like fun.

04:45.100 --> 04:47.220
Hey, where is the ship going?

04:48.670 --> 04:51.430
This ship is going to England to trade wine.

04:53.130 --> 04:55.750
Down the river to cross the ocean.
- Ocean?

04:56.650 --> 04:58.020
Wow!

04:58.770 --> 05:00.580
The ocean is big, isn't it?

05:00.970 --> 05:02.850
More than big.

05:03.200 --> 05:06.620
The Atlantic ocean especially, it's so big you can't see anything.

05:07.100 --> 05:10.560
It's a great feeling to board a ship and cross the ocean.

05:12.190 --> 05:14.990
Wow. I'd really like to see the ocean.

05:15.390 --> 05:18.630
Mr. Vitalis told me he'd take me to see it but...

05:19.620 --> 05:21.890
You've never seen the ocean?

05:22.420 --> 05:23.100
No.

05:23.480 --> 05:24.500
Oh, I see...

05:24.510 --> 05:26.870
Emile, what are you doing?! Hurry and get going!

05:27.230 --> 05:29.450
Agh, great. See you!

05:32.140 --> 05:35.180
Well, let's go home. Mr. Vitalis is waiting.

05:38.560 --> 05:39.860
You hungry?

05:40.320 --> 05:42.760
We have to wait until Remy and the others get back.

05:42.850 --> 05:43.890
I'm back!

05:48.450 --> 05:49.990
Took you long enough.

05:50.240 --> 05:54.670
Hey! Is there a place in this town where you can see the Atlantic Ocean?

05:54.950 --> 05:58.190
The Atlantic Ocean? Don't be silly.

05:59.410 --> 06:04.850
Come to think of it, there is a place where you can see the Atlantic and your hometown.

06:05.950 --> 06:06.610
Really?

06:25.080 --> 06:29.710
Not bad, eh?
- They're really well trained.

06:30.090 --> 06:32.930
I especially like the white dog.

06:36.590 --> 06:39.520
Some applause for our talented performers!

06:50.300 --> 06:50.900
Remy!

06:52.060 --> 06:55.280
Oh, Emile, how was the Vitalis Troupe?

06:55.700 --> 06:56.910
Very fun!

06:57.380 --> 07:00.900
It was great seeing the performance for the first time. I wish I could see it everyday.

07:01.850 --> 07:02.690
I'm glad.

07:03.460 --> 07:05.510
Come on, I'll show you the ocean.

07:07.030 --> 07:08.970
I found a place where you can see the ocean.

07:09.340 --> 07:10.760
Really?
- Yeah.

07:11.240 --> 07:14.150
I want to but Mr. Vitalis...

07:16.290 --> 07:17.920
We'll come back right away.

07:18.600 --> 07:20.060
But...
- Let's go!

07:33.110 --> 07:35.640
No, you have to go home.

07:35.790 --> 07:37.210
Let's take him with us.

07:37.580 --> 07:40.290
Capi can see the ocean too.
- Hey, Emile...

07:41.060 --> 07:43.880
Isn't that the smart dog from before?

07:44.300 --> 07:45.690
What a coincidence.

07:46.330 --> 07:48.050
What's he called?
- Capi.

07:48.200 --> 07:49.090
Ah, Capi.

07:52.520 --> 07:55.010
Heh, he's a really nice dog.

07:55.320 --> 08:02.440
Emile, don't go goofing off for long.
We set sail tomorrow, there's a lot to do.

08:09.170 --> 08:13.790
Your fellow sailors?
- Yeah, Victor and Gigi. Well, let's go.

08:18.930 --> 08:21.110
Wow, it's so tall.

08:21.710 --> 08:23.740
If we go on top of the tower we'll be able to see the ocean.

08:23.800 --> 08:25.670
Really? Let's hurry and climb it!

08:32.040 --> 08:33.790
They said you can't go in.

08:34.250 --> 08:37.560
Too bad they don't let dogs in.
- It can't be helped.

08:38.080 --> 08:41.990
Capi, wait for us here.
We'll be back soon, okay?

09:00.610 --> 09:02.680
Wow!
- Amazing!

09:04.670 --> 09:08.220
If you follow Garonne river...
that's where the ocean is.

09:12.030 --> 09:14.010
Huh? That's weird.

09:15.110 --> 09:16.660
I thought you could see it.

09:17.670 --> 09:23.530
Gigi said when he climbed up here, he could see the Atlantic Ocean and my hometown.

09:23.950 --> 09:25.250
Your hometown?

09:26.180 --> 09:28.580
Emile, what direction is Chavanon village?

09:28.670 --> 09:29.770
Chavanon village?

09:30.080 --> 09:31.320
My hometown.

09:31.780 --> 09:33.280
My mother and sister are there.

09:33.610 --> 09:35.480
I've never heard of that village.

09:36.030 --> 09:36.800
Oh.

09:39.510 --> 09:41.010
How did you get here?

09:41.670 --> 09:47.230
From Chavanon... we went to Ussel to buy clothes.

09:47.540 --> 09:49.570
Ussel is near my village!

09:50.090 --> 09:51.220
Ussel is in the East.

09:51.860 --> 09:54.770
And East is... umm... that way!

10:02.280 --> 10:03.360
Chavanon Village.

10:09.690 --> 10:12.910
I can't see them. I can't see mother or Nana.

10:18.680 --> 10:23.130
In my hometown, I also have a mother and younger siblings.

10:23.930 --> 10:25.410
I have a dog like Capi.

10:26.240 --> 10:27.740
His name's Petit...

10:28.910 --> 10:31.260
...because when we got him he was very small.

10:31.280 --> 10:33.490
Even when he grew up we still called him Petit.

10:34.770 --> 10:39.940
I didn't want to leave home but...
My father died and I couldn't work.

10:47.360 --> 10:48.110
Emile...

10:52.230 --> 10:53.750
I love the sea so it doesn't matter.

10:54.280 --> 10:58.090
I want to become a sailor quickly and travel around the world.

11:02.040 --> 11:04.150
Traveling isn't hard for you, Remy?

11:04.600 --> 11:09.250
It's not hard. Mr. Vitalis is very nice. We're always happy.

11:13.130 --> 11:16.890
But... I haven't forgotten my mother and Nana.

11:20.110 --> 11:21.940
Thank you, mother!

11:26.090 --> 11:27.340
Fine. Come on!

11:27.670 --> 11:28.290
Dear!

11:29.020 --> 11:30.270
Don't get involved!

11:34.260 --> 11:35.170
Remy...

11:46.190 --> 11:47.890
I'm sorry you couldn't see the ocean.

11:48.390 --> 11:50.130
No, it doesn't matter.

11:54.870 --> 11:56.720
Huh? Capi isn't here.

11:57.410 --> 11:58.110
Capi!

11:58.910 --> 11:59.720
Capi!

12:00.760 --> 12:01.970
Capi!

12:05.630 --> 12:08.890
Where could he have gone?
- He must've gone home.

12:22.310 --> 12:25.000
We wanted to see the ocean so we climbed the tower.

12:26.810 --> 12:30.670
When we came back though, we saw that Capi was missing.

12:30.950 --> 12:33.030
We thought he went back home but...

12:33.470 --> 12:36.270
Capi is a smart dog, he'll come back soon.

12:37.150 --> 12:40.920
Sorry for not telling you about leaving, before. I won't do it again.

12:47.770 --> 12:50.680
Capi, what's the matter? Come back quickly.

13:08.380 --> 13:09.920
There! There!

13:14.240 --> 13:16.710
This guy almost got away.

13:17.350 --> 13:18.300
I got him.

13:19.290 --> 13:23.040
Idiot! Don't let those dogs get away!

13:23.280 --> 13:25.490
The people on board will know what we're doing.

13:25.770 --> 13:28.640
It's not my fault, it's a bad dog!

13:28.970 --> 13:31.590
Shh! Don't be so loud!

13:33.660 --> 13:34.390
Let's go.

13:56.320 --> 13:58.220
Be quiet for once!

14:19.880 --> 14:20.570
Remy.

14:21.410 --> 14:22.000
Remy.

14:25.860 --> 14:27.640
Is Capi?
- Still not back.

14:29.520 --> 14:35.800
Capi is very responsible.
He wouldn't forget his work.

14:37.340 --> 14:43.400
I've heard of people stealing smart dogs to sell to the circus to make money.

14:44.440 --> 14:48.470
Then Capi is...
- It's not for sure.

14:49.130 --> 14:52.750
I'll go look for Capi with Dolce and Zerbino.

14:53.810 --> 14:55.640
I want to go too!
- No.

14:57.000 --> 15:00.530
Capi might come back when no one's here.

15:01.100 --> 15:03.060
You'll stay here.

15:04.140 --> 15:06.150
Let's go! Dolce, Zerbino!

15:16.330 --> 15:17.920
Joli-Coeur, what should we do?

15:18.380 --> 15:22.280
It's all... It's all my fault.
- Remy!

15:25.480 --> 15:27.460
Has Capi come back?
- No.

15:27.910 --> 15:30.330
Mr. Vitalis said he may have been captured.

15:31.150 --> 15:35.660
He said that there are people who capture dogs to sell to the circus.

15:36.660 --> 15:39.430
I saw a dog on the ship in the middle of the night.

15:40.690 --> 15:44.810
Maybe Capi has also...
been captured by Victor and Gigi.

15:45.580 --> 15:46.930
I want to go see.

16:13.440 --> 16:15.270
All right, one pair!

16:16.310 --> 16:17.390
This is bad.

16:18.030 --> 16:22.480
What is it?
- The keys. Victor locked the cabin.

16:22.830 --> 16:25.300
We have to get the keys.
- How?

16:25.300 --> 16:28.870
Yes! I won.

16:28.980 --> 16:33.240
Again, you always win.
- Stop complaining! Stop complaining!

16:33.650 --> 16:37.060
This isn't fun. I'm not playing.

16:51.910 --> 16:53.540
Are those the keys?
- Yes.

16:57.220 --> 16:59.600
Joli-Coeur, we need to borrow your talent.

17:00.020 --> 17:04.250
Bring us those keys.
Understand? The keys. Keys.

17:35.860 --> 17:38.900
All right! Lucky me!

17:41.740 --> 17:44.390
You did it, Joli-Coeur! You're so clever!

17:44.810 --> 17:45.380
Quickly!

18:02.280 --> 18:03.170
That's not it.

18:07.070 --> 18:07.730
It opened!

18:14.940 --> 18:15.620
Capi!

18:19.520 --> 18:20.840
We'll get you out now, Capi.

18:21.350 --> 18:25.250
Poor things. They've gone too far.
- How did you get in here?!

18:27.130 --> 18:30.060
What are you doing here?!
- You stole these dogs!

18:30.370 --> 18:32.030
I came to get Capi back!

18:32.040 --> 18:33.410
I can't let you do that.

18:34.470 --> 18:39.780
You'll be thrown overboard after we're out to sea or we'll sell you along with the dogs.

18:40.620 --> 18:43.860
Damn you!
- You little shit.

18:43.860 --> 18:45.820
Remy, run!
- Emile!

18:46.240 --> 18:47.910
Emile! Let him go!

18:48.590 --> 18:52.030
Shut up! Gigi! Hold this girl!

18:52.190 --> 18:52.780
Okay.

18:55.650 --> 18:56.770
Come here and be quiet!

19:00.030 --> 19:01.490
Stop struggling!

19:03.540 --> 19:04.200
Stop it you!

19:05.740 --> 19:06.780
Joli-Coeur!

19:07.930 --> 19:08.630
Damn it!

19:12.220 --> 19:13.190
Mr. Vitalis!

19:14.850 --> 19:16.210
Who are you!?

19:16.460 --> 19:18.240
Give me back my dog!

19:18.660 --> 19:21.440
Can't do that, old man.
- Victor!

19:22.080 --> 19:24.320
I do not allow fighting on my ship!

19:24.680 --> 19:27.390
Captain, there's a reason for this.
- Silence!

19:27.940 --> 19:29.480
What are these dogs doing here?

19:29.610 --> 19:34.090
You have dog thieves aboard your ship.
This dog is mine.

19:34.900 --> 19:38.100
Victor! You're really dispicable!

19:38.430 --> 19:40.770
Now I know what you've been doing!

19:41.080 --> 19:44.140
What do we do, Victor?
- Damn you!

19:47.910 --> 19:49.280
Catch him!

19:55.540 --> 19:57.250
Zerbino! Dolce!

20:01.570 --> 20:03.450
Let go! Let me go!

20:04.660 --> 20:05.610
Gotcha!

20:05.940 --> 20:08.980
Let go! Let me go!
- Stay still!

20:10.300 --> 20:11.210
Damn it!

20:12.750 --> 20:13.900
Mr. Vitalis!

20:15.040 --> 20:16.430
Are you all right, Remy?

20:16.850 --> 20:19.380
Yes, both me and Capi.

20:21.870 --> 20:23.640
And you too, Joli-Coeur.

20:23.920 --> 20:28.020
Must be nice, Remy's troupe is like a real family.

20:29.570 --> 20:34.240
Capi, Mr. Vitalis, and Remy all help each other.

20:34.840 --> 20:37.020
Just like a real family.

20:37.460 --> 20:38.450
Family?

20:52.070 --> 20:54.720
Goodbye! Take care!

20:55.050 --> 20:58.000
Emile, goodbye!

21:02.430 --> 21:05.100
See you later, Remy!

21:05.560 --> 21:10.100
Goodbye! Goodbye, Emile!

21:14.140 --> 21:16.410
Emile, I'll be fine.

21:16.980 --> 21:19.780
I miss mother and Nana but...

21:23.570 --> 21:25.290
I'm not alone.

21:27.180 --> 21:29.280
I have another family.

21:30.470 --> 21:32.030
Another family.

21:39.200 --> 21:47.750
Try to love yourself more

21:48.850 --> 21:57.710
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:58.420 --> 22:06.820
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:08.090 --> 22:18.720
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:19.420 --> 22:29.100
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:29.320 --> 22:38.950
From the future that gives us our fate

22:39.190 --> 22:47.220
Try to seek for them more

22:48.830 --> 22:52.350
Give your heart to

22:52.710 --> 23:07.390
That person who is also seeking you

23:19.160 --> 23:21.670
Oh, no! Fire!

23:22.030 --> 23:26.040
Mimi, there's a fire! Wake up!

23:29.560 --> 23:31.560
Our horse carriage!

23:32.420 --> 23:36.160
<i>Goodbye to Our Home</i>

23:32.420 --> 23:36.160
Next time:
